1
00:04:07,058 --> 00:04:13,058
Laugh or get off the pot.

2
00:08:14,117 --> 00:08:20,117
Tunnel Vision is a comedy film directed by Neal Israel.

3
00:12:21,176 --> 00:12:27,176
A committee investigating TV's first uncensored network examines a typical day's
programming, which includes shows, commercials, news programs, you name it.

4
00:16:28,235 --> 00:16:34,235
What they discover will surely crack you up!

5
00:20:35,294 --> 00:20:41,294
This outrageous and irreverent spoof of television launched the
careers of some of the greatest comedians of all time.

6
00:24:42,352 --> 00:24:48,352
Christian A. Broder, played by Phil Proctor.

7
00:28:49,411 --> 00:28:55,411
Senator McMannus, played by Howard Hesseman.

8
00:32:56,470 --> 00:33:02,470
Senator Polanski, played by Dan Barrows.

9
00:37:03,529 --> 00:37:09,529
Proctologist, played by Stephen Feinberg.

10
00:41:10,588 --> 00:41:16,588
Chevy Chase, played by Chevy Chase.

11
00:45:17,647 --> 00:45:23,647
Cooper, played by John Candy.

12
00:49:24,705 --> 00:49:30,705
TunnelVision (also known as Tunnel Vision) is a satirical 1976 comedy anthology film featuring Roger Bowen, Chevy Chase, John Candy, Howard Hesseman, Joe Flaherty, Laraine
Newman, Betty Thomas, Phil Proctor, Al Franken, Ron Silver, Tom Davis, and Michael Overly, with appearances by voiceover artists Ernie Anderson and Danny Dark.

13
00:53:31,764 --> 00:53:37,764
It was directed by Neal Israel and Bradley R.

14
00:57:38,823 --> 00:57:44,823
Swirnoff and produced by Joe Roth.

15
01:01:45,882 --> 01:01:51,882
Although the title is repeatedly displayed in the film as being spelled "Tunnelvision",
it is frequently identified as "Tunnel Vision" in home video reissues.

16
01:05:52,941 --> 01:05:58,941
The tone is lighthearted.
